                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I think it might be a good idea to also add some tests in `common/test/pldm_utils_test.cpp` as proof that this work"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure. Added few test cases covering various scenarios. Let me know if any other test case is required to be added."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 392,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe we could remove the `transform` and use `UCS-2BE` directly, without roundtriping to Host endian and back to what iconv expect.\n\n(we could also perhaps drop the `std::u16string` and just construct an `std::u16string_view` argument directly to avoid copying and allocation\n\n```cpp\nstd::optional<std::string> utf16ToUtf8(std::u16string_view u16Str);\n\nauto nameString = pldm::utils::utf16ToUtf8({ decodedPdr->names[count].name, u16NameStringLen });\n```\n\nbut we are already doing this in the current code, so feel free to ignore)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 392,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "That definitely makes things simpler. I've updated the implementation to pass the big-endian data directly to iconv using \"UCS-2BE\" as the source encoding, eliminating the be16toh() roundtrip entirely. \nAlso switched from std::u16string to std::u16string_view to avoid unnecessary copies as suggested."
                }
            ],
