                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "return std::nullopt instead of empty string"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 969,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Dropped u16Str.empty() check as iconv handles zero-length input as a no-op, so the function naturally falls through to return with an empty string."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 969,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 975,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "seems like libpldm currently exposes the raw buffers, which means callers end up dealing with wire-format details like endianness themselves. That seems to be why we have assumptions around big-endian UCS-2 in the conversion logic here.Not sure if this was already discussed as part of a different commit but @andrew@codeconstruct.com.au Would it make sense to eventually have helper APIs in libpldm for parsing/normalizing these fields .I think that could help keep this kind of logic out of the callers and make usage a bit less error-prone."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 975,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please review https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/88801 :)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 982,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "an early exit before calling iconv_close() might leak the conversion descriptor"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 982,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Wrapped iconv_open's result in a std::unique_ptr with iconv_close as the deleter. Removed both explicit iconv_close(cd) calls as any early return between open and final use can no longer leak the descriptor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 982,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.hpp",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "utils.hpp is a common header included in a lot of files. I would suggest moving this inclusion to utils.cpp since that's the only place we need this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.hpp",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Moved it to utils.cpp"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.hpp",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.hpp",
                    "line": 768,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "this seems like we are leaking the wire format assumptions into the generic utility function in pldm ? are we lacking some function in libpldm that can handle that ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.hpp",
                    "line": 768,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "lipldm has a handful of UTF-16 helpers, but I'm not sure if they're helpful in this scenario."
                }
